its influence. Starting instead from 1010's only contact 1429 also fails to reach 883, and all nodes involved are low-degree with the relevant activity dying out after roughly t=75316."}, "raw_final_response": "## Findings\n\n**1010 cannot originate any cascade in this window.** Its only interaction is a single *inbound* event (1429\u21921010) \u2014 zero out-edges (step_04, step_05, step_07, step_09). A cascade requires the source to emit at least one contact; there is no first hop to build on.\n\n**Failure is not an artifact of the 600-unit gap constraint.** Reachability fails identically at max_wait=600 (step_01), max_wait=5000 (step_15), and with no wait limit at all (step_02) \u2014 in every case `n_nodes_reached = 1`, i.e. the frontier never leaves the source. Enumeration returns zero routes (step_13).\n\n**Confounder controls:**\n- *Ambient volume:* the window is busy (6,477 events, 1,922 active nodes, 6,271 distinct edges \u2014 step_03), so absence reflects the specific temporal structure, not a sparse or empty window.\n- *Static connectivity:* the 3-hop neighbourhood of 1010 is large and richly connected (step_08), and 883 is reachable when direction/time are ignored via 1209\u2192883 (step_14). So an undirected, time-blind path exists \u2014 yet it carries no influence.\n- *Relaxing the source:* even starting from 1010's actual contact 1429, 883 is unreachable (step_10), so the failure isn't a one-node quirk.\n- *Node popularity:* the endpoints and broker are low-activity (1010: 1 event; 883: 2; 1429: 4; 1209: 11 \u2014 step_04, step_11), and 883's two events involve only 1038 and 1209 (step_06). Activity is scattered across bins with the trio going silent after ~75316 (step_12), leaving no ordered chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_20982933\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 1429, 1209, 1038],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1010 to 883 exists. Node 1010 has exactly one interaction in the window and it is inbound (1429->1010), giving it no outgoing first hop. Temporal reachability returns reached=false with only the source in the reached set at max_wait=600, at max_wait=5000, and with no wait constraint, and path enumeration yields zero routes \u2014 so the negative result is driven by directed temporal structure, not by the 600-unit gap threshold. Confounders are excluded: the window is highly active (6477 events, 1922 nodes), 1010's 3-hop static neighbourhood is large, and an undirected time-blind connection to 883 exists through 1209, yet none of this transmits influence. Starting instead from 1010's only contact 1429 also fails to reach 883, and all nodes involved are low-degree with the relevant activity dying out after roughly t=75316.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 39952, "total_output_tokens": 3611, "total_tokens": 43563, "total_latency_ms": 60354, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}